From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:28:30 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 27/45] Plutonium: agent keyboard focus beside the user's; the
 compositor decorates every window

EXO-AGENT: a client can keyboard-focus a window for an agent while the
user's focus is in another app (Seat::AddAgentFocus()). Its keyboards
focus its most recent agent surface when the user's focus isn't in the
client; the user's keys still follow aura focus, and the agent's keys and
modifier changes go only to the target. InjectKeyEvents() adds the agent
focus for its keys instead of borrowing the seat's focus (still done when
the user's focus is in another window of the same app), and
EmbeddedWindows::HoldAgentFocus() keeps it between calls, over DevTools
as Plutonium.setWindowAgentFocus. An app that moves its own focus after a
key only while focused (Enter in Writer's style box) now does.

EXO-DECOR: xdg-decoration always answers server_side, and Exo implements
KDE's server-decoration protocol (what GTK 3 reads), always answering
server, so apps draw no title bars or borders of their own.
